      "oracle": "a paste event on the product page reaches the DOCUMENT: it advances the revision, and the pasted text appears EXACTLY ONCE in the ODT the product saves afterwards -- the document, not the toast. Exactly once, not merely present: the sink also sees `beforeinput` with insertFromPaste, so a page-level paste handler that fails to cancel the event commits the same text twice, and `in` would call that a pass",
